=== PIPELINE_DESIGN ===
normalize.Pipeline is THE ONE entry between codec.Atomic and the typed
per-destination writers. Process(ctx, payload, vehicleIntID) -> error
calls codec.Decode (errors wrapped as ErrPayloadDrop), then
processAtomics:
  1. sortAtomicsSettingUnitFirst (sort.SliceStable by IsSettingUnit)
  2. for each atomic:
       Setting*Unit -> observeSettingUnit -> histRepo.Record(SourceTelemetry)
       else         -> toSI -> router.Route
toSI looks up the active unit at atomic.EmittedAt via histRepo.At and
calls units.ToSI(field, raw, active). UnitKindCharge fields and
dimensionless fields pass through unchanged. ErrNotFound from histRepo.At
becomes ErrNoUnitContext (drop + UnitContextMissing metric).

Routable interface (subset of *router.Router) lets the test suite supply
a fake without populating the empty routing.yaml from Prompt 0025.
A compile-time assert (var _ Routable = (*router.Router)(nil)) keeps the
production wiring lockstep.

=== INVARIANT_TEST ===
TestSettingUnitProcessedFirstInSamePayload locks the SettingUnitFirst
reordering: VehicleSpeed BEFORE SettingDistanceUnit in input -> repo.ops
sequence is [record(distance,km), at(distance,t)]; speed is converted
with the freshly-Recorded km row to 27.7 * 1000/3600 = 7.6944 m/s.
TestSinglePipelineInvariant uses go/parser + go/ast to assert the only
exported method on *Pipeline returning error is Process, and no other
package-level exported function returns error.

